ves Heyward a chance to  be involved and maybe screening and  catching the past well there it is out  to Heyward cut it right here  and I was told just to make a play I  like going left more than anything so I  tried to go this way  same worth defending ten seconds ago he  wants to drive and coming up and I went  behind the back and drove behind the  back the whole time I knew I'm gonna  shoot this and zubik pops out right here  I was able to use my height all 72 of me  and actually affect the play in a  positive way on the baseline makes me  step back but I arc it a little bit more  than I normally would  three point six seconds you know I  missed it that walk back to the other  free-throw line was one of the longest  walks I've ever experienced now sit back  put the line to a couple dribbles made  the first one about the shoot the second  one and briefly look over and let's get  the signal to miss it says missing  Coach K elected to have him miss the  second one to not give Butler a chance  to run a set plate it is a risk right  because then it stays a two-point game  missing that free-throw though does put  a lot of pressure on you to get the ball  up the court quickly you don't win  something big without taking some risk  you just don't want it to be Gamble's  I didn't gamble I wrist Heyward had  already made a game-winner in this state  high school championship game and had  already proven to be an outstanding  clutch player in this situation let's  see what they got lined up here you know  we're down 12.1 seconds left and you  know we have to go the length of the  court I like to get the ball thingy work  somehow  honestly I was definitely back of my  mind this very similar situation with  the chance to win national title game in  Indianapolis  I can definitely remember thinking here  we go again let's do it again  that young man right there at a Milan  moment do you believe in sequels  certainly looks that way better partner  my goodness we've always put Gord